result.proposedFix:
Filter out ticks that fall outside the axis's current scale extent in `Axis#getTicksCoords`, before mapping them to coords — i.e. fix it at the source of the coords, not inside `fixOnBandTicksCoords`. Restrict the filter to the ordinal scale, because that is the only tick path that is cached (and therefore the only one that can go stale), and its tick values/extents are integers so the comparison is exact.

Replace the `map(...)` block at src/coord/Axis.ts:179-188 with:

```ts
        const scale = this.scale;
        const isOrdinal = scale.type === 'ordinal';
        // The ticks of a category axis are cached (see `axisTickLabelBuilder`),
        // so they may have been made for a wider scale extent than the current
        // one (for example, before dataZoom narrowed the window). Those ticks
        // are out of the visible window and would be rendered outside the grid,
        // so discard them here. Ticks of the other scale types are always made
        // from the current extent.
        const scaleExtent = scale.getExtent();
        const ticksCoords: TickCoord[] = [];
        for (let i = 0; i < ticks.length; i++) {
            const tickVal = ticks[i];
            if (isOrdinal && (tickVal < scaleExtent[0] || tickVal > scaleExtent[1])) {
                continue;
            }
            ticksCoords.push({
                coord: this.dataToCoord(
                    isOrdinal ? (scale as OrdinalScale).getRawOrdinalNumber(tickVal) : tickVal
                ),
                tickValue: tickVal
            });
        }
```
(the rest of `getTicksCoords` — `alignWithLabel` lookup and the `fixOnBandTicksCoords(this, ticksCoords, alignWithLabel, opt.clamp)` call — stays untouched, so clamp:true semantics for splitLine/splitArea are preserved).

Why here and not elsewhere (measured, variant-by-variant):
- Verified numerically against a replica of the current algorithm. This fix ('B') yields exactly the values the regression test wants: non-clamp [0,100,200,300] and clamp [0,100,200,300] with coords[0]===extent[0]===0 and last===extent[1]===300; it also cleans up the redundant/duplicated ticks (window [1,3] -> [0,100,200,300] instead of [0,100,200,300,300]) and window [3,3] -> [0,300] (correct single band) instead of six ticks at 150.
- The alternative of looping the clamp removal inside `fixOnBandTicksCoords` (variant 'A': `while (ticksCoords.length > 1 && !littleThan(axisExtent[0], ticksCoords[1].coord)) ticksCoords.shift();` + symmetric pop) also satisfies the two failing assertions, but measurably does NOT fix `boundaryGap:false` ([-300,-150,0,150,300] unchanged) nor `alignWithLabel:true` ([-150,-50,50,150,250] unchanged), because that function early-returns for those. So it is a strictly weaker fix.
- Fixing it in `createAxisTicks`/`makeCategoryTicks` would require either mutating/copying the memoized array on every call (perf-sensitive path for large category data) or extending the cache key with the extent; filtering at the consumer keeps the cache untouched.
- No change is needed in `getMinorTicksCoords`: `scale.getMinorTicks()` is recomputed from the live extent and produced no out-of-extent coords in any probe.

Non-regression evidence for 'does not change non-zoomed charts': across the whole 4300+ config chart sweep (all axis types, all filterModes, inverse, min/max/scale/minInterval/interval/splitNumber, customValues, singleAxis, polar, y/both-axis zoom, before and after 6 different dataZoom actions), zero ordinal ticks ever fell outside `scale.getExtent()` — so the filter is a provable no-op for freshly built axes. Nine fresh-axis tick configurations (interval 0/1/2, count 1/2/5, alignWithLabel, onBand=false, inverse, clamp on/off) produce byte-identical coord arrays with and without the filter.
